Assignment 1.03 - Distance Maps

Hello TA,

This implementation of assignment 1.03 creates distance maps for the hiker and rival NPCs using Dijkstra's algorithm.

The movement costs for each PC/NPC are stored in a lookup table in character.c, this way we can access that information faster. Like the professor recommended, we store boulders and trees as a seperate terrain type with infinite cost to act as a natural blocker for all PC/NPC types. This implementation uses a min-heap with decrease priority to meet the needs of the assignment. Finally, Dijkstra's uses that priority queue to create the distance maps for both rivals and hikers to the PC.

I wrote this is a way where you may move between maps still (like 1.02) and generate new distance maps for that map you move to.

If there are any questions feel free to reach me at griffinu@iastate.edu


